{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK4qwSHVTAN5eE31YkaJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed it by changing one line, `django/db/models/sql/compiler.py:35`. The regex that strips `ASC`/`DESC` from each `ORDER BY` term now has the `re.MULTILINE | re.DOTALL` flags:\n\n```python\nself.ordering_parts = re.compile(r'(.*)\\s(ASC|DESC)(.*)', re.MULTILINE | re.DOTALL)\n```\n\n**Cause:** `.` didn't match newlines, so for a multiline `RawSQL` the regex only captured the last line before `ASC`/`DESC`. `get_order_by()` uses that captured text to spot duplicate ordering terms. Two different expressions that ended with the same line (like `else null end`) were treated as duplicates, and the second was dropped.\n\n**Fix:** With `DOTALL`, `.` matches newlines, so the whole SQL expression is captured and compared. Expressions that only share their last line are no longer seen as duplicates.\n\nThe `expressions`, `ordering` and `queries` test modules pass: 513 tests, 10 skipped, 2 expected failures. I didn't run the issue's three-`RawSQL` query myself, and I didn't add a test because the rules don't allow editing test files."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":231,"cache_read_input_tokens":19550,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":231},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"605fe91e-fd5a-49a2-a655-ef8009bd9449","uuid":"80446963-382f-4f09-ba5f-04aca1fec612","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:25:33.451Z","request_id":"req_011ChK4qw5DBhVEtGqt4u3xS"}
